& [ClarifiedIntent]
  + SJS builds the SOP that governs one declared problem space
  + the SOP carries optimized inference hints that remain present for all turns and all interdependent jobs within the scope of their justification
  + SJS also governs how the active frame may forget by sampling gradual diffusions that can reconstruct the stable operative frame
  + repeated controlled release should minimize the active attention basis without losing the governed subject intention constraints dependencies receipts or frontier
  + released experience can remain in exact custody and narrative even when it leaves the immediate attention projection

& [SelectedNames]
  + ScopeWideHintCovenant binds which source-grounded hints must be projected into every inference call and job within one JustificationScope
  + RestorationTestedAttentionBasis is the bounded active projection currently admitted for that scope
  + ControlledForgettingPass proposes one strictly smaller candidate basis and tests it before release
  + OperativeFrame is the exact subject intention authority constraints dependency state latest accepted receipts unresolved frontier and stop conditions that must remain stable
  + RestorationWitness binds candidate basis recovery-source identities reconstructed frame comparison and disposition
  + MinimumRecoverableFrame is a restoration-tested attention basis for which no permitted single release or bounded candidate reduction passes the declared equivalence policy

& [TypedSJSAndSOPLevels]
  + Level0 SJSFormation consumes preserved source and produces a signed governing execution SOP with exact hint scope retention recovery comparison and evidence rules
  + Level1 GovernedSOPExecution projects the admitted basis into every covered turn and job executes the work records semantic events and may propose controlled forgetting
  + Level2 SuccessorSOPProposal may describe a revised SOP but cannot govern until it reenters a separately valid SJS admission and satisfaction-signature gate
  + an execution SOP cannot widen its own authority alter its governing invariants or admit its own successor
  + these typed levels terminate self-authorization even when an SOP performs work that generates another SOP proposal

& [JustificationScope]
  + scope binds governing source identities subject and purpose job set turn interval model and provider profile tool policy authority ceiling and completion or invalidation conditions
  + common hints apply to every job and turn in scope while job-local stitches may be added without removing the common covenant
  + a job leaving reentering splitting or joining the pool preserves the common scope identity and receives the current admitted basis
  + scope drift authority drift source invalidation conflicting receipt or changed completion conditions force recompilation or stop

& [CompiledHintCovenant]
  + SJS classifies hints as mandatory governing anchor mandatory denial mandatory open obligation stable relation recoverable coordinate optional trajectory cue or expired item
  + mandatory anchors denials and open obligations have nonzero retention floors while applicable
  + every hint binds source intended transform applicability completion invalidation and restoration role rather than remaining a bare term
  + the compiled SOP defines where the covenant is projected how its identity is checked and how a job proves which revision it received

& [ControlledForgettingPass]
  + begin from admitted basis B0 and one exact OperativeFrame F0
  + select only release-eligible hints under a deterministic bounded policy and produce a strictly smaller candidate basis B1
  + reconstruct candidate frame F1 from B1 plus the exact recovery sources permitted by the governing SOP
  + compare F1 with F0 under the compiled FrameEquivalencePolicy
  + admit B1 only when every mandatory identity invariant dependency receipt frontier and stop condition is conserved and the result is anchored
  + refuse the release and restore the removed hints when the result is drifted or underdetermined
  + append an immutable RestorationWitness and forgetting receipt for either outcome
  + repeat from the latest admitted basis until no permitted smaller candidate passes or the bounded pass budget is exhausted

& [DiffusionMeaning]
  + diffusion is the ordered series B0 B1 through Bn of candidate active projections and their restoration witnesses
  + it is not an uncontrolled fade inside model weights logits attention heads or K/V cache
  + a signal may lose immediate projection strength while the exact source event and recovery coordinate remain retained outside the model call
  + reverberation is the reconstruction and comparison cycle that tests whether the smaller projection still regenerates the operative frame needed for the next step

& [FrameEquivalencePolicy]
  + exact-equality fields include scope source authority policy model and provider identities where declared job identities latest receipt coordinates and checkpoint identities
  + set-conservation fields include applicable constraints denials open requirements dependencies evidence obligations unresolved frontier and stop conditions
  + semantic correspondence fields such as purpose and intended transform require a governed public comparison rule and may not rely on unreviewed model confidence
  + newly inferred material must remain proposed and cannot make a reconstruction anchored unless separately supported
  + multiple reconstructed frames compatible with the retained evidence yield underdetermined rather than an arbitrary winner

& [MinimumBoundary]
  + minimum initially means locally irreducible under one exact deterministic candidate generator release granularity pass budget and equivalence policy
  + global mathematical minimality is not claimed unless a finite candidate space is exhaustively searched and independently replayed
  + a minimum frame is scope model task horizon and policy specific and must be invalidated when those identities drift
  + byte count token estimate and hint count are measured separately because the smallest serialized basis may not produce the lowest execution cost

& [NarrativeRelationship]
  + admitted semantic events forgetting proposals restoration witnesses receipts releases failures reentries and scope transitions form the exact narrative source ledger
  + NarrativeProjection tells how the working frame changed and why a cue remained refreshed decayed released or returned
  + narrative detail may remain larger than the active basis and can help human reentry without being projected into every inference call
  + narrative is an attributed public account and never a capture of hidden chain of thought

& [OptimizationHypothesis]
  + source-grounded lookahead hints can reduce agent decision entropy irrelevant retrieval repeated reads plan repair and time to correct operation
  + restoration-tested minimization can reduce context bytes or tokens while retaining accepted semantic and authority correspondence
  + raw per-token model computation speed context-window widening and a three-to-five-times gain remain experimental claims
  + compare unminimized covenant static hand summary uncontrolled term decay and controlled forgetting under equal tasks models providers tools budgets and acceptance gates

& [FirstProviderFreeDirection]
  + compile supplied ScopeWideHintCovenant OperativeFrame candidate basis recovery-source and FrameEquivalencePolicy values
  + perform deterministic single-removal and bounded grouped-removal passes over synthetic fixtures
  + independently replay every RestorationWitness and prove monotone size exact refusal and locally irreducible disposition
  + adversaries include mandatory-hint release source substitution stale checkpoint omitted job dependency receipt rollback frontier loss semantic alias collision ambiguous reconstruction self-authorizing successor and narrative-as-authority laundering

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes exact source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical schema equivalence rule minimality proof satisfaction signature Rust implementation prompt projection provider call model output durable storage autonomous work SOP activation successor admission workspace mutation remote host FPGA Minecraft physical effect or performance claim is authorized
